    "findings": [
      "isTaskEffect belongs here and task-effect.fungi recognizes exactly eight case-sensitive strings through two helper flows. The asset covers membership only, not parsing, permissions, dependencies, execution or reporting; tests cover all eight accepted and five rejected strings.",
      "load-tasks parsing uses regex searches and brace counting without string/comment awareness. Malformed unfinished blocks stop extraction, unknown effects are silently filtered, numeric properties accept digit prefixes without safe-integer bounds, and first-match/trimming/list splitting/duplicate-task/optional-field behavior is observable.",
      "checkTaskPermissions has first-error ordering: shell unsafe flag, unsafe reason, shell permission, filesystem checks, environment checks, network, database. Path checks are lexical and do not establish resolved-path or symlink containment; network/database/shell values are nonempty-only, while compiler/reports/crypto effects have no matching permission gate.",
      "runTask checks permissions even for dry runs, returns failed on denial, dry-run when requested and otherwise skipped; it performs no task operations, dependency execution, timeout enforcement or shell sandboxing. dryRunTask itself bypasses permission validation.",
      "resolveTaskDependencies uses last-wins duplicate definitions, breadth-first relevant-task discovery and external graph ordering; preserve missing-dependency precedence, cycle diagnostics, duplicate-edge behavior and task identity.",
      "Task reports retain input references and copy errors including internalDiagnostic. safeMessage is not response redaction. Result lookup is first-wins, while aggregate status considers all results including those absent from displayed dependency order; generatedAt defaults to wall clock.",
      "The scoped load-tasks row remains BLOCKED:SCOPED_CANDIDATES_ONLY with evidence digest fcd476bfb7e88c8f6d980e43dd58587bfdf3a882ca63ec71121fd7f63a0e9db1; this does not authorize broader package translation."
    ],
    "materialObligations": [
      "Preserve parser regex/brace, malformed-input, effect filtering, numeric, duplicate and optional-field semantics or explicitly narrow the language contract.",
      "Preserve permission ordering, lexical path behavior, effect coverage gaps, unsafe-shell requirements and dry-run versus execution placeholder behavior.",
      "Preserve dependency graph ordering, missing/cycle diagnostics, duplicate definitions/edges and task identity.",
      "Preserve report reference/error retention, first-wins result lookup, aggregate status and wall-clock defaults; do not infer redaction from safeMessage.",
      "Keep task-effect.fungi non-authorizing, retain TypeScript shadow and do not admit externally owned symbols isResponseSafeClassification or validateTransition into this package."
    ]
  },
